 Locale definitions   | MIT                         | /usr/share/licenses/musl-locales/
 Keyboard definitions | GPL-2.0 family              | /usr/share/licenses/kbd/

Note: grep, gzip, tar and vi fall under BusyBox's GPL-2.0-only as long as they
are provided as BusyBox applets. Installing the GNU versions adds their own
licenses (mostly GPL-3.0-or-later). bash is not bundled by default
(GPL-3.0-or-later; the user may install it).


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Japanese Environment (enable this section when the components are bundled)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Japanese environment is defined as a requirement but is not bundled in
this release. In a release that starts bundling it, add the components below,
install their full license texts under /usr/share/licenses/, and then enable
this section.

 Component            | License                     | Location of full license text
----------------------+-----------------------------+--------------------------------
 Mozc                 | BSD-3-Clause                | /usr/share/licenses/mozc/
 Mozc dictionary data | BSD-3-Clause                | /usr/share/licenses/mozc/
 IBus                 | LGPL-2.1-or-later           | /usr/share/licenses/ibus/
 Fcitx5               | LGPL-2.1-or-later           | /usr/share/licenses/fcitx5/
 Noto Sans CJK JP     | SIL OFL 1.1                 | /usr/share/licenses/noto-cjk/
 Noto Serif CJK JP    | SIL OFL 1.1                 | /usr/share/licenses/noto-cjk/
 IPAex fonts          | IPA Font License 1.0        | /usr/share/licenses/ipaex-fonts/


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Summary of License Terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(1) GPL-2.0-only / GPL-2.0-or-later

    - Redistributing the source code requires providing the complete
      corresponding source code.
    - The full license text and copyright notices must be retained.
    - No additional restrictions may be imposed on redistribution.
    - The corresponding source of the components covered here that are part of
      this ISO can be obtained by the method described in section 7 below.

(2) GPL-3.0-or-later

    - In addition to the obligations in (1), installation information may have
      to be provided for some products.
    - No additional patent restrictions may be imposed.

(3) LGPL-2.1-or-later

    - The full license text and copyright notices must be included.
    - The corresponding source must be provided; if the library was modified,
      it must be provided in a form that allows relinking.

(4) MIT / BSD-2-Clause / BSD-3-Clause / ISC / OpenSSH license

    - The copyright notice and the full license text must be included.
    - BSD-3-Clause includes a condition against using the copyright holder's
      name for promotional purposes.

(5) SIL OFL 1.1

    - The full license text must be included.
    - The fonts may not be sold on their own.
    - A modified version may not use the original Reserved Font Name.

(6) IPA Font License 1.0

    - The full license text must be included.
    - Modification and redistribution are subject to the terms of that license.

(7) Files under multiple licenses

    - For dual-licensed components such as less, check the notice in the same
      directory to see which license was applied.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Obtaining the Corresponding Source Code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For the components covered by the GPL and LGPL, SabakanOS provides the complete
corresponding source code. This includes the configuration files used for the
build (config/kernel-defconfig, config/buildroot-defconfig), any patches, and
the build scripts.

  Distribution page:
    https://github.com/ryotagtagtag-wq/sabakan-os/releases

  Each release is published with the following files:
    - sabakanos-<version>-x86_64.iso
    - sabakanos-<version>-source.tar.zst      <- the complete corresponding source
    - COPYING                                 <- this file
    - SHA256SUMS                              <- hashes of all attached files

  For details on how to obtain the source and on the manifest format, see
  docs/source-flow.md in the repository.

  If you cannot obtain the source by the method above, contact us at the
  address below. Under a written offer, we provide a complete copy of the
  corresponding source code for three years from the date of distribution.

  The source is provided from the same server as the binary, which satisfies
  the requirements of GPL-2.0 section 3(a), GPL-3.0 section 6(a) and
  LGPL-2.1 section 4. Redistributors of this ISO must offer the same source to
  their own recipients.


